    """Returns True if any of the tests in the bitfield test are
    True. For example, `(G_FILE_TEST_EXISTS | G_FILE_TEST_IS_DIR)`
    will return True if the file exists; the check whether it's a
    directory doesn't matter since the existence test is True. With
    the current set of available tests, there's no point passing in
    more than one test at a time.

    Apart from GLib.FileTest.IS_SYMLINK all tests follow symbolic links,
    so for a symbolic link to a regular file GLib.file_test() will return
    True for both GLib.FileTest.IS_SYMLINK and GLib.FileTest.IS_REGULAR.

    Note, that for a dangling symbolic link GLib.file_test() will return
    True for GLib.FileTest.IS_SYMLINK and False for all other flags.

